@startuml C4-Dynamic-Globe-Bootstrap
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

title Dynamic — Globe bootstrap (createGlobe → dispose)

actor "Browser User" as user
participant "Theme Page\n(React)" as page <<ui>>
participant "createGlobe\n(infra/three)" as globe
participant "GlobeRoot" as root
participant "LandDotsGroup" as land
participant "FlightArc /\nRouteMarker" as arc
participant "WebGL Canvas" as canvas

user -> page: 1. Open /globe-light or /globe-dark
page -> globe: 2. createGlobe(container, canvas, { theme, colors })
globe -> root: 3. new GlobeRoot(theme, colors)
root -> land: 4. LandDotsGroup(themeId, config)
land --> root: 5. materials[]
root -> arc: 6. FlightArc / RouteMarker (per DEFAULT_ROUTES)
arc --> root: 7. meshes
globe -> canvas: 8. requestAnimationFrame (root.tick)
globe --> page: 9. GlobeHandle { materials, state, dispose }
page --> user: 10. Interactive globe

note right of page
  On unmount: handle.dispose()
  stops rAF and removes listeners
end note

user -> page: 11. Leave route / unmount
page -> globe: 12. dispose()

@enduml
